id: 17
hanzi: 扇子
pinyin: shàn zi
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Noun

meanings_summary:
  en: fan (handheld folding or round fan); device creating cool breezes
  es: abanico; pai-pai; abano; instrumento de mano para refrescarse

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Noun | Standard | a handheld device made of paper, silk, bamboo, or feathers used to agitate the air and generate a cooling breeze | instrumento de mano de papel, seda, bambú o plumas para agitar el aire y refrescarse | 摇动扇子 (wave a fan)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 盛夏的傍晚，老人们喜欢坐在弄堂的大槐树下，一边摇着蒲扇，一边惬意地闲话家常。 | Shèngxià de bàngwǎn, lǎorénmen xǐhuan zuò zài lòngtáng de dà huáishù xià, yìbiān yáo zhe púshàn, yìbiān qièyì de xiánhuà-jiācháng. | On midsummer evenings, elders like sitting beneath the alley's large locust tree, comfortably chatting about daily life while waving palm leaf fans. | Al atardecer en pleno estío, los ancianos gustan de sentarse bajo las acacias del callejón, charlando plácidamente de la vida cotidiana mientras agitan sus abanicos de palma.
  #2 | 摸象故事中摸到大象宽大耳朵的盲人，立刻斩钉截铁地大呼大象明明就是一把随风摇摆的扇子。 | Mō xiàng gùshì zhōng mōdào dàxiàng kuāndà ěrduo de mángrén, lìkè zhǎndīng-jiètiě de dàhū dàxiàng míngmíng jiùshì yì bǎ suífēng yáobǎi de shànzi. | In the fable, the blind man who touched the elephant's broad ear immediately shouted unequivocally that an elephant was simply a fan swaying in the wind. | En la fábula, el ciego que rozó las anchas orejas del elefante exclamó tajante que el animal era a todas luces un abanico que ondeaba al viento.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  一把扇子 | a fan (classifier: 把)
  摇扇子 | wave a fan
  折叠扇子 | folding fan (折扇)
  纸质扇子 | paper fan
  羽毛扇子 | feather fan (羽扇)
  收起扇子 | fold or put away a fan

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  羽扇纶巾 | yǔ shàn guān jīn | feather fan and silk kerchief; poised, graceful demeanor of a strategist
  秋风见扇 | qiū fēng jiàn shàn | a fan discarded in autumn breeze; neglected after outliving utility
  摇扇纳凉 | yáo shàn nà liáng | wave a fan to enjoy the cool breeze
  扇风点火 | shān fēng diǎn huǒ | fan the flames; incite trouble and stir up discord

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  扇 | shàn | fan; flap wings; door leaf | abanico; batir alas; batiente | 户 | single door / household | 户 (single door leaf swinging open) | 羽 (yǔ, feathers / wings) | 10 | 半包围结构 | Ideogram combining door leaf 户 and wings/feathers 羽, representing a swinging leaf that beats breezes like birds' wings. | Under the door frame (户), feathered wings (羽) flutter back and forth to create a cooling handheld fan (扇). | Bajo el marco de la puerta (户), un haz de plumas (羽) se bate con suavidad para engendrar la brisa del abanico (扇). | 51 | HSSMM | 
  子 | zi | child; son; noun suffix | hijo; niño; sufijo nominal | 子 | child / son | 子 (swaddled baby) | "" | 3 | 单一结构 | Universal noun suffix designating everyday utensils and household objects. | A lively infant (子) waves its hands happily in the cool summer breeze. | Un niño vivaz (子) mueve las manitas alegre al sentir la brisa del verano. | 214 | ND | 

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: A door flap (户) adorned with fluttering feathers (羽) creates the refreshing breeze of a summer fan (扇子).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Una batiente de puerta (户) guarnecida de plumas (羽) agita el aire fresco del abanico tradicional (扇子).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In classical Chinese literati culture, fans (折扇, 团扇) were not merely functional cooling tools, but canvas mediums for calligraphy, landscape painting, and poetry, carried as essential emblems of scholastic poise (文人雅士之信物).
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Falling 4th tone followed by neutral tone: 'shàn zi' (51-neutral). Articulate 'shàn' with crisp downward momentum and pronounce 'zi' lightly.

